.TH QFW-COMPILE 1 "November 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Commands"
.SH NAME
qfw-compile \- compile circuits for a device from its snapshot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-compile
.BI --snapshot " device.json"
.BI --in " circuits.qpy"
.BI --out " compiled.qpy"
.RI [ --compiler " qiskit|mqt" ]
.RI [ --optimization-level " n" ]
.RI [ --seed-transpiler " n" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-compile
compiles the circuits in a QPY file for the device a snapshot recorded, checks
them against it, and marks them for it, as
.B QFwBackend.compile
does against a live QPM. It needs no QPM, no DEFw and no reservation, so it can
run in a CPU job ahead of the job that runs the circuits. A snapshot is the JSON
that
.B QFwBackend.device_snapshot()
returns.
.PP
A QPM refuses a marked circuit whose calibration the device has since left,
under its
.BR calibration-policy .
Call
.B backend.check_isa()
first in the run job to find that out before the queue wait.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero when every circuit compiled. Nonzero when a circuit cannot be compiled for
the device or a file cannot be read.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-setup (1),
.BR qfw-srun (1),
.BR qfw (7)
